<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hemadri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Hemadpant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hemadri, also known as Hemadpant, was minister to the Seuna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadava">Yadava</a> kings Mahadeva and Ramachandra in the 13th century. He compiled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaturvarga-chintamani">Chaturvarga Chintamani</a>, a great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> digest of religious law, and wrote on medicine and other subjects. Tradition credits him with the Hemadpanti style of stone temples built without mortar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>.</p></div>
